# vibe-acp 2.26.1 (mistral-vibe, scratch VIBE_HOME and workspace under bwrap, with the environment unharness starts it with: VIBE_SMART_APPROVE_AVAILABLE=true and VIBE_AGENT_PATHS naming the directory where unharness wrote unharness-ask.toml and unharness-accept-edits.toml) via scripts/record-acp.py --client-capabilities '{"elicitation":{"form":{}}}' --config mode=unharness-ask --fork --deny --close --cancel-after 90 "Remember the code word mango. Reply with OK." "Write the code word into the file word.txt.": --config sets the mode option to unharness-ask before the first prompt (sent unanswered, as the driver sends options; its answer reads unharness-ask back). After that turn --fork forks the session while it is open in the same process: session/fork answers at once with a new id and the source's mode (unharness-ask), and the fork's usage starts at zero. The fork's turn knows the code word; its write_file and then a bash command are asked about by toolCallId alone and denied, and nothing is written. session/close closes the fork. No stderr lines were written (none to strip).
